__REVIEW_PROFILE__

PROJECT: mock3 — two independent TypeScript codelines sharing the same stack.
- mock-a (`/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a`): fare logic. Source in `src/fares.ts`, tests in `test/fares.test.ts`. Key exports: `fareFor(rider: Rider)`, `totalFor(riders: Rider[])`, types `Rider`, constants `BASE_FARE_CENTS`, `CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS`.
- mock-b (`/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b`): departure board. Source in `src/schedule.ts`, tests in `test/schedule.test.ts`. Key exports: `formatStops(stops: Stop[])`, `totalMinutes(stops: Stop[])`, type `Stop`.

STACK CONVENTIONS (both codelines identical):
- ESM (`"type": "module"`), TypeScript `strict: true`, `target: ES2022`, `moduleResolution: bundler`.
- Test runner: vitest. Tests use `import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'`. Run tests with `npm test` (executes `vitest run`).
- Type-check / build: `npm run build` (executes `tsc --noEmit`). There is no lint step.
- Source lives under `src/`, tests under `test/`, both included in `tsconfig.json`.
- No external runtime dependencies; devDependencies only are vitest and typescript.

KNOWN BUG PATTERNS IN THIS PROJECT:
- MOCK3-1 (fare logic): boundary comparison uses `>` where `>=` is required — riders aged exactly 65 fall through to the base fare instead of the concession fare. When reviewing, confirm the comparison operator is `>=` and that a test case for `age === 65` exists.
- MOCK3-2 (departure board): `formatStops` loops `i < stops.length - 1`, which skips the final stop. When reviewing, confirm the loop bound includes the last index and that a test asserts the last stop name appears in the output.

